42":43,"_44":43,"_45":197,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":50,"_51":119,"_53":198,"_55":199,"_57":200,"_59":201,"_61":202,"_63":203,"_65":204,"_67":205,"_69":43,"_70":71},{"_30":177,"_32":178,"_34":179,"_36":180,"_38":181,"_40":182,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":183,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":52,"_51":152,"_53":184,"_55":185,"_57":186,"_59":-5,"_61":187,"_63":188,"_65":189,"_67":190,"_69":43,"_70":71},{"_30":161,"_32":162,"_34":89,"_36":163,"_38":164,"_40":165,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":166,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":167,"_55":168,"_57":169,"_59":-5,"_61":170,"_63":171,"_65":172,"_67":173,"_69":43,"_70":71},{"_30":146,"_32":147,"_34":132,"_36":148,"_38":149,"_40":150,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":151,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":152,"_51":153,"_53":95,"_55":-5,"_57":154,"_59":-5,"_61":155,"_63":156,"_65":157,"_67":158,"_69":43,"_70":71},{"_30":130,"_32":131,"_34":132,"_36":133,"_38":134,"_40":113,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":135,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":50,"_51":136,"_53":137,"_55":138,"_57":139,"_59":-5,"_61":140,"_63":141,"_65":142,"_67":143,"_69":43,"_70":71},{"_30":109,"_32":110,"_34":89,"_36":111,"_38":112,"_40":113,"_42":114,"_44":115,"_45":116,"_47":117,"_48":118,"_49":119,"_51":119,"_53":120,"_55":121,"_57":122,"_59":123,"_61":124,"_63":125,"_65":126,"_67":127,"_69":43,"_70":71},{"_30":87,"_32":88,"_34":89,"_36":90,"_38":91,"_40":92,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":93,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":94,"_51":50,"_53":95,"_55":95,"_57":96,"_59":-5,"_61":97,"_63":98,"_65":99,"_67":100,"_69":43,"_70":71},{"_30":31,"_32":33,"_34":35,"_36":37,"_38":39,"_40":41,"_42":43,"_44":43,"_45":46,"_47":43,"_48":43,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":54,"_55":56,"_57":58,"_59":60,"_61":62,"_63":64,"_65":66,"_67":68,"_69":43,"_70":71},"id","193","name","The Roman Colosseum","type","landmark","startDescription","An iconic symbol of ancient Rome, this amphitheater hosted gladiatorial contests and public spectacles.","endDescription","It remains a testament to Roman engineering and a major tourist attraction today.","startYear",-70,"startMonth",0,"startDay","endYear",80,"endMonth","endDay","startSignificance",0.9,"endSignificance",0.7,"imageUrl","https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Colosseo_2020.jpg/330px-Colosseo_2020.jpg","imageCredit","FeaturedPics / Wikimedia Commons / CC BY-SA 4.0","sourceUrl","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colosseum","cdnId","images/2146ac274cf2f2ac1f73e14f17dc2a1e3f33a444.webp","country",{"_32":84,"_85":86},"subjects",[78,79],"group",{"_32":75,"_76":77},"user",{"_30":72,"_73":74},"likes","liked",false,"6","username","HistOracle","Ancient Rome","icon","GiColiseum",{"_30":82,"_32":83},{"_30":80,"_32":81},"9","art","3","culture","Italy","continent","Europe","1133","Marcus Anthony","person","A prominent figure in Roman history, known for his military prowess and political alliances during the late Republic.","His life concluded with a significant defeat, marking the end of his influence in Roman politics.",-83,-30,0.8,"","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Anthony",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[103,104],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":101,"_73":102},"7","Kushim",{"_30":107,"_32":108},{"_30":105,"_32":106},"2","politics","1","military","313","Julius Caesar","A pivotal figure in the transition from the Roman Republic to the Roman Empire, he played a critical role in the events that led to the demise of the Republic.","His assassination marked a turning point in Roman history, leading to the rise of his adopted heir.",-100,7,12,-44,3,15,1,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Retrato_de_Julio_C%C3%A9sar_%2826724093101%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Retrato_de_Julio_C%C3%A9sar_%2826724093101%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","España / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Caesar","images/9b5ca30be4dc787c3d598b5006cfb5f022433617.webp",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[128,129],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":107,"_32":108},{"_30":105,"_32":106},"2418","Roman Ballista and Onager","event","Romans standardized torsion artillery for both field and siege use.","Integrated artillery into permanent fortifications and legions.",300,0.85,"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_ballista.jpg","Roman ballista reconstruction / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballista",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[144,145],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":107,"_32":108},{"_30":82,"_32":83},"1129","Roman Tuba","The Roman Tuba was a brass instrument used primarily in military contexts, signaling troops and enhancing the martial atmosphere.","As the Roman Empire transitioned, the Tuba's military significance diminished, leading to its eventual obsolescence.",-200,500,0.5,0.2,"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuba_(instrument)",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[159,160],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":107,"_32":108},{"_30":82,"_32":83},"916","Hannibal Barca","A military commander from Carthage, he is best known for leading his forces, including war elephants, across the Alps to invade Italy during the Second Punic War. His tactical genius is still studied in military academies around the world.","His life ended in exile, and he left a lasting legacy as one of history's greatest military strategists.",-247,-183,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Hannibal_Barca_bust_from_Capua_photo.jpg/330px-Hannibal_Barca_bust_from_Capua_photo.jpg","Image: Hannibal / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hannibal",{"_32":175,"_85":176},[174],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":101,"_73":102},{"_30":107,"_32":108},"Tunisia","Africa","1364","Gladiators","period","Fighters who engaged in combat for public entertainment in ancient Rome, often slaves or prisoners of war.","The practice of gladiatorial combat faded as the Roman Empire declined and Christianity rose, leading to its eventual prohibition.",-264,404,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Gladiators_from_the_Zliten_mosaic_3.JPG/330px-Gladiators_from_the_Zliten_mosaic_3.JPG","Image: Gladiator / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gladiator",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[191,192],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":107,"_32":108},{"_30":82,"_32":83},"189","The Punic Wars","A series of three wars fought between Rome and Carthage, pivotal in establishing Rome as a dominant power in the Mediterranean.","The conclusion of the wars resulted in the complete destruction of Carthage and the expansion of Roman territory.",-146,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Domain_changes_during_the_Punic_Wars_BC.gif/330px-Domain_changes_during_the_Punic_Wars_BC.gif","Carnby / Wikimedia Commons / CC BY-SA 4.0","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punic_Wars","images/748c7f2c104b560733aea2dd524348f36960b1f8.webp",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[206,207],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":107,"_32":108},{"_30":105,"_32":106},"2388","Roman Gladius","Short sword used by Roman legions for stabbing in close combat.","Iconic weapon of the Roman military, shaping European sword design.",-300,"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Gladius.png","Image: Roman Gladius / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gladius",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[220,221],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":107,"_32":108},{"_30":82,"_32":83},"1267","Roman Roads","Rome began building paved, durable roads around 300 BCE to support military movement, communication, and trade across its expanding territories.","The vast road network unified the empire, enabling rapid troop travel and economic integration. Its engineering principles shaped infrastructure for centuries.","https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Roman_roads_around_Rome.png/330px-Roman_roads_around_Rome.png","Image: Roman roads / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_road",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[233,234],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":101,"_73":102},{"_30":107,"_32":108},{"_30":235,"_32":236},"4","intellectual","1272","Aqua Appia","This was the first aqueduct built in ancient Rome, designed to transport water from springs to the city, showcasing advanced engineering techniques.","The aqueduct fell into disrepair over the centuries but remains a significant example of Roman engineering.",-312,0.3,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Aqua_appia_planlatium_2.png/330px-Aqua_appia_planlatium_2.png","Image: Aqua Appia / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_Appia",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},"1546","Roman Republic","This era marked the establishment of a new form of government, characterized by a complex system of checks and balances, and a focus on civic duty and public service.","The transition to imperial rule signaled the end of the Republic, leading to a centralized autocratic governance under a single ruler.",-509,-27,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Roman_republic%2C_territory_44_BC.svg/330px-Roman_republic%2C_territory_44_BC.svg.png","Image: Roman Republic / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Republic",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[263,264],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":105,"_32":106},{"_30":82,"_32":83},"2238","Samnite Confederation","The Samnite Confederation was a group of tribes in central and southern Italy known for their resistance to Roman expansion during the Samnite Wars.","The confederation was eventually defeated and incorporated into the Roman Republic by the late 3rd century BCE.",-600,-290,0.4,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Samnite_Territory.png/330px-Samnite_Territory.png","Image: Samnite territory / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samnites",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[279],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":82,"_32":83},"1545","Roman Kingdom","This era marks the foundation of one of history's most influential civilizations, characterized by its early political structures and cultural developments.","The period concluded with the establishment of the Roman Republic, marking a significant shift in governance and societal organization.",-753,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Platner_-_Ancient_Rome_city_growth.jpg/330px-Platner_-_Ancient_Rome_city_growth.jpg","Image: Roman Kingdom / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Kingdom",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[292,293],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":105,"_32":106},{"_30":82,"_32":83},"964","The Etruscan Civilization","This civilization flourished in ancient Italy, known for its rich culture, art, and influence on Roman society. It was characterized by unique burial practices and vibrant frescoes.","The civilization gradually declined as Rome expanded, leading to the assimilation of Etruscan culture into Roman traditions.",-800,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Etruscan_civilization_map.png/330px-Etruscan_civilization_map.png","Image: Etruscan civilization / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etruscan_civilization",{"_32":84,"_85":86},[306],{"_32":75,"_76":77},{"_30":72,"_73":74},{"_30":82,"_32":83},[],"subject",[],[],"yearStart",-300000,"yearEnd",2025,"search","sortBy",true]
